From blackwel at fas.harvard.edu  Wed Sep 21 17:58:01 2011
From: blackwel at fas.harvard.edu (Matt Blackwell)
Date: Wed, 21 Sep 2011 17:58:01 -0400
Subject: [amelia] observation-level priors and log transformations
In-Reply-To: <4C9FA51CB843EC44B99194310A8C0DF015619B@UWIT-MBX08.exchange.washington.edu>
References: <4C9FA51CB843EC44B99194310A8C0DF015619B@UWIT-MBX08.exchange.washington.edu>
Message-ID: <EC297E52A0F44041968AB5564DB61876@gmail.com>

Hi Joe,  

The priors are not transformed, so they refer to the transformed variable (that is, log(tariff), rather than tariff). This is because the normal priors on the observation make more sense when the distribution is itself normal, which is usually after the log transformation. Hope that helps.  

Cheers,
matt.

